1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,919
In this series we build the UI for a small
game called Coin Shop, from an empty

2
00:00:05,919 --> 00:00:06,468
project.

3
00:00:06,468 --> 00:00:12,162
A main menu, a store, a top bar and a nav
bar shared by both, and a purchase popup.

4
00:00:12,162 --> 00:00:13,877
One short step per video.

5
00:00:13,877 --> 00:00:14,700
Let's start.

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,932
Open the Package Manager, press plus, and
choose Add package from git URL.

7
00:00:20,932 --> 00:00:24,308
Paste the address from the docs and press
Add.

8
00:00:24,308 --> 00:00:28,786
Unity installs the framework, and
Addressables comes with it.

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:46,332
Every screen will be an Addressable scene,
so open Addressables Groups once and

10
00:00:46,332 --> 00:00:47,808
create its settings.

11
00:00:47,808 --> 00:00:53,862
Set the play mode script to Use Asset
Database, so screens load straight from
your

12
00:00:53,862 --> 00:00:55,929
project when you press Play.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,459
This window is where you'll build all of
your UI.

14
00:01:04,459 --> 00:01:07,691
In the General tab, press Create Config.

15
00:01:07,691 --> 00:01:12,054
The config remembers where your scripts
and scenes go.

16
00:01:12,054 --> 00:01:18,760
Set the two namespaces to your game's:
Coin Shop dot UI dot Elements, and Coin
Shop

17
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,214
dot UI dot States.

18
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,153
Below are the Global Canvas Settings.

19
00:01:28,153 --> 00:01:33,102
Every new screen starts with these: a
portrait phone at ten-eighty by

20
00:01:33,102 --> 00:01:36,042
nineteen-twenty, scaling with the screen.

21
00:01:36,042 --> 00:01:39,771
Change them here once, and every new
screen follows.

22
00:01:39,771 --> 00:01:43,500
Existing screens are never changed behind
your back.

23
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:54,100
That's the setup, and you only do it once.

24
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,929
Next, we create our first screen.
